/ "before each goal" and "before goal Process" both run for Process, in the order they were bound. Each is the
/ "each goal" event's call and One the named one's; One is a goal too, so the "each goal" event runs before it as well.
Start
- set %ran% = ""
- before each goal, call Each
- before goal Process, call One
- call Process
- assert %ran% equals "each,each,one,", "each goal first, then the one bound on Process, in the order bound"

/ The goal both events run before.
Process
- set %done% = "yes"

/ The "each goal" event's call.
Each
- set %ran% = "%ran%each,"

/ The "before goal Process" event's call.
One
- set %ran% = "%ran%one,"
